{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Strange Stories", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Night in Jail", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Relate information about common solutions to problems in spoken or written documents. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect Tense vs. Past Simple ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect</span>:  </li><li>For something that started in the past and continues in the present. </li></ul> Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> I have been married for ten years.</span> <br><br> </li><li>For something that has been done several times. </li></ul>Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">She has sung that song a lot of times. I love it!!  </span> <br> <br></li><li>For experiences up to the present. </li></ul> Example: <br><span class=\"italic\">This is the worst experience I've ever had.</span> <br><br></li><li> For something that happened in the past but is relevant at the time of speaking. </li></ul>  Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> I can't get into the hotel. I've lost my key. </span> <br> <br> </li><li>For referring to a time that is not yet finished. </li></ul> Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">They have bought a new house this week.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\"> Simple Past</span>: <br></li><li>  For something that was finished at a certain period of time. </li></ul>  Example: <br>  <span class=\"italic\">The architect finished the building in 1990.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sentence\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" When?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> When we arrived at the Carleton County Gaol, the 150-year-old building looked less formidable than I imagined. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" when we arrived\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">They looked golden-rose in the evening light.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" the night we stayed there\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I have never slept in jail.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" at any time in my life\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The stone and brick walls have weathered well.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" over the years since they were built\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Surprisingly, I have visited several old jails in the past. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They haven't turned the cells into luxury suites.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Although they have upgraded a little.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The hostel has become well-known by the adventurous. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My boyfriend surprised me with an impromptu visit to Ottawa to do just that.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This one was rather quaint in comparison.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We sat in a lounge to relax, had complimentary breakfast arrive at our cell door in the morning and of course there was WiFi too! ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Gerunds and Infinitives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> is a verb ending with -ing (doing).<br/>An <span class=\"strong\">infinitive</span> is to + verb (to do).", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are some verbs that can only be followed by a gerund:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "appreciate (doing)<br/>can't help (doing)<br/>enjoy (doing)<br/>spend time (doing)<br/>consider (doing)<br/>dream about (doing)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">appreciate having</span> new experiences.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A phrasal verb is always followed by a gerund.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">If you've <span class=\"strong\">dreamed about roughing</span> it in a cell, this is the place to come.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There are some verbs that can only be followed by an infinitive:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "strive (to do)<br/>hesitate (to do)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I wouldn't <span class=\"strong\">hesitate to</span> recommend it. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Spending time sitting</span> in a jail cell was hardly at the top of my list.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">can't help feeling</span> a little closed in though.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She <span class=\"strong\">enjoyed scaring</span> us with tales of ghosts.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We didn't <span class=\"strong\">consider staying</span> again that night!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The owners have strived <span class=\"strong\">to retain</span> a feeling of authenticity in the cells.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "jail", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a prison", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have never slept in jail.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about a night in jail.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "impromptu", "type": "name"}, {"content": "done without preparation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My boyfriend surprised me with an impromptu visit to Ottawa to do just that. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "at the top of my list", "type": "name"}, {"content": "first of the things that I want to do", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Spending time sitting in a jail cell was hardly at the top of my list.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "formidable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "inspiring fear", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The 150-year-old building looked less formidable than I imagined.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to weather", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to change from being exposed to the weather", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The stone and brick walls have weathered well.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "quaint", "type": "name"}, {"content": "old-fashioned charm", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This one was rather quaint in comparison.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to strive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to try hard", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They strived to keep their customers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "authenticity", "type": "name"}, {"content": "genuine; as it was originally", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The owners have strived to retain a feeling of authenticity in the cells.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "barred", "type": "name"}, {"content": "enclosed with bars", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Even the old barred doors are still in place. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob09aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Look up the Lockup - a prison-themed restaurant in Japan or another themed restaurant or hotel and read or watch a video about it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make notes about the themed restaurant or hotel.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write up a description of the place.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use verb plus infinitive and verb plus gerund as often as you can.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your description aloud to a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I look up a themed restaurant or hotel and make notes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a description of the themed restaurant or hotel.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use verb plus infinitive and verb plus gerund where I can.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my description with a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn9le05ob09re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn9le05ob09re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "I have never slept in jail, but my boyfriend surprised me with an impromptu visit to Ottawa to do just that. I appreciate having new experiences, but spending time sitting in a jail cell was hardly at the top of my list.<br/><br/>When we arrived at the Carleton County Gaol, the 150-year-old building looked less formidable than I imagined. Surprisingly, I have visited several old jails in the past. This one was rather quaint in comparison.  The stone and brick walls have weathered well. They looked golden-rose in the evening light."}, {"image": "engenn9le05ob09re2img02.jpg", "time": "33000", "id": 2, "text": "The owners have strived to retain a feeling of authenticity in the cells. Even the old barred doors are still in place. You can't help feeling a little closed in though. They haven't turned the cells into luxury suites. Although they have upgraded a little. We sat in a lounge to relax, had complimentary breakfast arrive at our cell door in the morning and of course there was wifi too!"}, {"image": "engenn9le05ob09re2img03.jpg", "time": "58000", "id": 3, "text": "In the morning we went on a free tour. A guide took us all around the heritage building. She enjoyed scaring us with tales of ghosts who supposedly walk there. Needless to say, we didn't consider staying again that night!<br/><br/>The hostel has become well-known by the adventurous. I wouldn't hesitate to recommend it. If you've dreamed about roughing it in a cell but haven't got a lot to spend, this is the place to come. I had a great time!"}], "audiosrc": "engenn9le05ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le05ob09re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": "engenn9le05ob09re3img01.jpg", "type": "img"}], "id": 2}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": "engenn9le05ob09re4img01.jpg", "type": "img"}], "id": 3}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": "engenn9le05ob09re5img01.jpg", "type": "img"}], "id": 4}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "ty